Here's the complete HTML document for a sorting algorithm visualizer with a dark theme, animated bars, and the required programmatic API.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Sorting Visualizer</title>
    <style>
        *,
        *::before,
        *::after {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        body {
            background-color: #0f0f1a;
            color: #e0e0e0;
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .app {
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 850px;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 20px;
        }

        .header {
            text-align: center;
        }

        .header h1 {
            font-size: 1.6rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: 0.03em;
            color: #c0c0d0;
            margin-bottom: 4px;
        }

        .header .subtitle {
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            color: #707080;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        #bars {
            display: flex;
            align-items: flex-end;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 2px;
            height: 400px;
            background: #161625;
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 16px 12px;
            border: 1px solid #252535;
            box-shadow: inset 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .bar {
            flex: 1;
            min-width: 2px;
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #4ecdc4 0%, #38b2a7 100%);
            border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0;
            transition: height 0.08s ease, background 0.12s ease;
            box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(78, 205, 196, 0.25);
        }

        .bar.comparing {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ff6b6b 0%, #e55555 100%);
            box-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(255, 107, 107, 0.55);
            z-index: 2;
        }

        .bar.sorted {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #6bff8e 0%, #4ade6a 100%);
            box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(107, 255, 142, 0.35);
        }

        .controls {
            display: flex;
            gap: 12px;
            justify-content: center;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
        }

        button {
            padding: 12px 28px;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: 0.04em;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.2s ease;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            outline: none;
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        button:active {
            transform: scale(0.96);
        }

        #sort {
            background: #4ecdc4;
            color: #0a0a14;
        }
        #sort:hover {
            background: #5eddd4;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(78, 205, 196, 0.4);
        }
        #sort:disabled {
            background: #2a3a38;
            color: #556;
            cursor: not-allowed;
            box-shadow: none;
        }

        #shuffle {
            background: #ff6b6b;
            color: #0a0a14;
        }
        #shuffle:hover {
            background: #ff7f7f;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(255, 107, 107, 0.4);
        }

        #reset {
            background: #3d3d55;
            color: #d0d0d0;
        }
        #reset:hover {
            background: #4d4d68;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(100, 100, 140, 0.3);
        }

        .status-bar {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 16px;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: #707080;
            min-height: 24px;
        }

        .status-bar .step-count {
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
            font-family: 'SF Mono', 'Consolas', 'Monaco', monospace;
            color: #9090a0;
        }

        .status-bar .done-badge {
            background: #1a3a1a;
            color: #6bff8e;
            padding: 3px 10px;
            border-radius: 20px;
            font-weight: 600;
            font-size: 0.75rem;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            opacity: 0;
            transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
        }
        .status-bar .done-badge.visible {
            opacity: 1;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="app">
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Sorting Visualizer</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Bubble Sort &middot; Step by Step</p>
        </div>
        <div id="bars"></div>
        <div class="status-bar">
            <span class="step-count" id="stepDisplay">Steps: 0</span>
            <span class="done-badge" id="doneBadge">SORTED</span>
        </div>
        <div class="controls">
            <button id="sort">▶ Sort</button>
            <button id="shuffle">🔀 Shuffle</button>
            <button id="reset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        (function() {
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // DOM references
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            const barsContainer = document.getElementById('bars');
            const sortBtn = document.getElementById('sort');
            const shuffleBtn = document.getElementById('shuffle');
            const resetBtn = document.getElementById('reset');
            const stepDisplay = document.getElementById('stepDisplay');
            const doneBadge = document.getElementById('doneBadge');

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // State
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            const DEFAULT_SIZE = 30;
            let currentArray = [];
            let initialArray = [];
            let sortState = {
                i: 0,
                j: 0,
                completed: false,
            };
            let totalSteps = 0;
            let animationId = null;
            let isAnimating = false;

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Helpers
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            function isSorted(arr) {
                for (let i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {
                    if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1]) return false;
                }
                return true;
            }

            function shuffleArray(arr) {
                const a = arr.slice();
                for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
                    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
                    [a[i], a[j]] = [a[j], a[i]];
                }
                return a;
            }

            function createPermutation(n) {
                const arr = [];
                for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) arr.push(i);
                return shuffleArray(arr);
            }

            function resetSortState() {
                if (currentArray.length <= 1 || isSorted(currentArray)) {
                    sortState.i = 0;
                    sortState.j = 0;
                    sortState.completed = true;
                } else {
                    sortState.i = 0;
                    sortState.j = 0;
                    sortState.completed = false;
                }
                totalSteps = 0;
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Rendering
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            function renderBars() {
                // Ensure correct number of bar elements
                const existing = barsContainer.children;
                const needed = currentArray.length;

                while (existing.length < needed) {
                    const bar = document.createElement('div');
                    bar.className = 'bar';
                    barsContainer.appendChild(bar);
                }
                while (existing.length > needed) {
                    barsContainer.removeChild(barsContainer.lastChild);
                }

                if (needed === 0) return;

                const maxVal = Math.max(...currentArray, 1);
                const bars = barsContainer.children;

                // Determine which indices to highlight
                let highlightA = -1;
                let highlightB = -1;
                if (!sortState.completed && needed > 1) {
                    highlightA = sortState.j;
                    highlightB = sortState.j + 1;
                }

                for (let i = 0; i < needed; i++) {
                    const heightPercent = (currentArray[i] / maxVal) * 100;
                    bars[i].style.height = heightPercent + '%';
                    const isComparing = (i === highlightA || i === highlightB);
                    bars[i].classList.toggle('comparing', isComparing);
                    bars[i].classList.remove('sorted');
                }

                // If fully sorted, mark all bars as sorted
                if (sortState.completed && needed > 0) {
                    for (let i = 0; i < needed; i++) {
                        bars[i].classList.add('sorted');
                        bars[i].classList.remove('comparing');
                    }
                }

                // Update status display
                stepDisplay.textContent = 'Steps: ' + totalSteps;
                if (sortState.completed) {
                    doneBadge.classList.add('visible');
                } else {
                    doneBadge.classList.remove('visible');
                }
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Sort step (bubble sort)
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            function sortStep() {
                const n = currentArray.length;

                // Already sorted or trivially sorted
                if (sortState.completed) {
                    return true;
                }
                if (n <= 1) {
                    sortState.completed = true;
                    renderBars();
                    return true;
                }

                // Perform one comparison
                const j = sortState.j;
                if (currentArray[j] > currentArray[j + 1]) {
                    // Swap
                    [currentArray[j], currentArray[j + 1]] = [currentArray[j + 1], currentArray[j]];
                }

                totalSteps++;

                // Advance indices
                sortState.j++;
                const limit = n - sortState.i - 1;
                if (sortState.j >= limit) {
                    sortState.j = 0;
                    sortState.i++;
                    if (sortState.i >= n - 1) {
                        sortState.completed = true;
                    }
                }

                renderBars();

                return sortState.completed;
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Animation
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            function stopAnimation() {
                if (animationId !== null) {
                    clearTimeout(animationId);
                    animationId = null;
                }
                isAnimating = false;
                sortBtn.disabled = false;
            }

            function startAnimation() {
                stopAnimation();

                // Reset sort state to beginning
                resetSortState();
                renderBars();

                if (sortState.completed) {
                    // Already sorted – nothing to animate
                    return;
                }

                isAnimating = true;
                sortBtn.disabled = true;

                const delay = Math.max(8, Math.min(40, Math.floor(600 / currentArray.length)));

                function step() {
                    if (!isAnimating) return;
                    const done = sortStep();
                    if (!done) {
                        animationId = setTimeout(step, delay);
                    } else {
                        // Animation complete
                        animationId = null;
                        isAnimating = false;
                        sortBtn.disabled = false;
                    }
                }

                animationId = setTimeout(step, delay);
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Public API (on window.viz)
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            window.viz = {
                array() {
                    return currentArray.slice();
                },

                setArray(a) {
                    stopAnimation();
                    currentArray = a.slice();
                    resetSortState();
                    renderBars();
                },

                sortStep() {
                    // If animation is running, stop it (manual stepping takes over)
                    if (isAnimating) {
                        stopAnimation();
                    }
                    return sortStep();
                },

                sorted() {
                    return isSorted(currentArray);
                },
            };

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Button handlers
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            sortBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
                if (isAnimating) {
                    stopAnimation();
                    return;
                }
                if (isSorted(currentArray) && sortState.completed) {
                    // Already sorted – reset and re-sort for demonstration
                    resetSortState();
                    renderBars();
                }
                startAnimation();
            });

            shuffleBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
                stopAnimation();
                currentArray = shuffleArray(currentArray);
                resetSortState();
                renderBars();
            });

            resetBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
                stopAnimation();
                currentArray = initialArray.slice();
                resetSortState();
                renderBars();
            });

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Initialization
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            function init() {
                currentArray = createPermutation(DEFAULT_SIZE);
                initialArray = currentArray.slice();
                resetSortState();
                renderBars();
            }

            init();
        })();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```
### Sorting Visualizer

This tool visualizes array comparisons and swaps with animated bars, sort controls, and a console API for manual testing.

- **The Core Algorithm**: The visualizer uses **Bubble Sort**. Each call to `sortStep()` performs exactly one comparison (and a potential swap) between two adjacent bars. This step-by-step approach lets you watch the process unfold or control it programmatically.

- **How to Interact**:
    - **Buttons**: Use **Sort** to animate the entire sorting process, **Shuffle** to randomize the array, and **Reset** to return to the initial shuffled state.
    - **Visual Feedback**: During sorting, the two bars being compared turn red. Once the array is fully sorted, all bars turn green.
    - **Programmatic Control**: For testing, you can call `window.viz.setArray([...])` with a known array, then repeatedly call `window.viz.sortStep()` until `window.viz.sorted()` returns `true`. The bars will update with each step.

- **Visual Style**: The interface features a consistent dark theme. Bar heights are proportional to their numerical values, and smooth CSS transitions are applied to height changes, making swaps visually clear and fluid.
